From 20087a43bc01a73efb00d9579f3dc68a790dbb7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <107831991+SyntaxError-PEBKAC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:13:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] ducksteps: notify when a newer release is published

The updater is disabled in ducksteps builds, so users had no way to
learn that a new release exists. Add DuckstepsReleaseCheck, which once
a day reads tag_name from the GitHub "latest release" API response and
compares it with the running version. Drafts and pre-releases are
ignored, and the tag must look like a plain version number.

When a newer version exists, a notification bar offers Download (opens
that release's page on the ducksteps repository) and Not now (hides the
bar until the next version). The About dialog shows the same status.
The link is built from the validated version, never taken from the
response, so it cannot point outside the ducksteps repository.

Nothing is downloaded or installed. Disable with
ducksteps.releasecheck.enabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
